## The Door Below

::bg{location="harbor" time="night"}
::music{playback="change" mood="sad" volume="down" assetId="music.tense"}
::actor{character="mara" anchor="left" action="fadeIn" emotion="sad" costume="raincloak"}
::actor{character="elio" anchor="right" action="fadeIn" emotion="worried" costume="coat"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: The tide lowers, revealing a door beneath the pier.
@mara{code="0010" emotion="sad"}: We closed the lantern, but not the story.
@elio{code="0010" emotion="worried"}: We can come back when we are ready.
@mara{code="0020" emotion="angry"}: I was ready three years ago.
@elio{code="0020" emotion="hopeful"}: You are ready now. That is different.
@narrator{code="0020"}: Mara places the compass on the threshold.
@mara{code="0030" emotion="worried"}: If Liora is behind this door, she will know we came.
@elio{code="0030" emotion="neutral"}: And if she is not?
@mara{code="0040" emotion="sad"}: Then we learn to carry the question.
@narrator{code="0030"}: The blue ribbon catches on a nail and points toward the dark.
@mara{code="0050" emotion="hopeful"}: Tomorrow, we return.
@elio{code="0040" emotion="happy"}: Tomorrow, I bring two umbrellas.
@narrator{code="0040"}: The sea answers with a patient knock.
::cg{assetId="cg.lighthouse" display="show" layout="inset"}
@mara{code="0060" emotion="hopeful"}: Some doors close to keep us safe.
::cg{assetId="cg.lighthouse" display="hide"}
::music{playback="stop"}
::actor{character="mara" action="fadeOut"}
::actor{character="elio" action="fadeOut"}
@narrator{code="0050"}: Dusk ending.
